{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 1]], "date-time": "2026-02-01T04:17:01Z", "timestamp": 1769919421859, "version": "3.49.0"}, "reference-count": 61, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "2", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 19]], "date-time": "2024-11-19T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1731974400000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["Plant Breeding"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2025, 4]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>ABSTRACT</jats:title><jats:p>Fusarium head blight (FHB) is a disease that affects all cereals worldwide. This includes emmer wheat (<jats:styled-content style=\"fixed-case\"><jats:italic>Triticum turgidum</jats:italic></jats:styled-content> ssp. <jats:italic>dicoccum</jats:italic>), the ancestor of durum and bread wheat. We screened 143 cultivated emmer genotypes from a breeding program and gene bank collections for FHB severity at 2 locations over 2\u2009years. Due to the high negative correlation between FHB severity and heading date (HD) (<jats:italic>r</jats:italic>\u2009=\u2009\u22120.65, <jats:italic>p</jats:italic>\u2009&lt;\u20090.001), plot\u2010level FHB scores were corrected for HD before further analysis (FHB<jats:sub>corr</jats:sub>). Genetic variation for FHB severity was high, ranging from 2.15 to 8.33 on a 1\u20139 scale. Twelve genotypes carried the semi\u2010dwarfing <jats:italic>Rht\u2010B1b</jats:italic> marker allele, which reduced plant height by 32\u2009cm but increased FHB severity by 20%. Genome\u2010wide association study detected seven quantitative trait nucleotides (QTNs) for FHB<jats:sub>corr</jats:sub> and three QTNs for plant height. The most important QTN for both traits was located on chromosome 4B, explaining 50.9% and 15.8% of the phenotypic variation in plant height and FHB<jats:sub>corr</jats:sub>, respectively, and was localized near the semi\u2010dwarfing <jats:italic>Rht\u2010B1</jats:italic> locus. Three other large\u2010effect loci for FHB<jats:sub>corr</jats:sub> were found on chromosomes 5B and 7B. In total, 72.6% of phenotypic variation was explained by all markers. The use of <jats:italic>Rht\u2010B1b</jats:italic> in emmer breeding has a high effect on plant height but would entail the introgression of potent FHB\u2010resistance from either native or exotic sources.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1111/pbr.13247", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 20]], "date-time": "2024-11-20T03:59:03Z", "timestamp": 1732075143000}, "page": "273-284", "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1, "title": ["Marker Effects for Fusarium Head Blight Resistance and the Dwarfing Gene <i>Rht\u2010B1</i> in Cultivated Emmer Wheat (<scp><i>Triticum turgidum</i></scp> ssp. <i>dicoccum</i>) Revealed by Association Mapping"], "prefix": "10.1111", "volume": "144", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9541-3726", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Thomas", "family": "Miedaner", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "State Plant Breeding Institute University of Hohenheim  Stuttgart Germany"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1020-4133", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Muhammad", "family": "Afzal", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "State Plant Breeding Institute University of Hohenheim  Stuttgart Germany"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0403-035X", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Laura", "family": "Morales", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Institute of Biotechnology in Plant Production  Tulln an der Donau Austria"}, {"name": "Department of Forest Genetics and Plant Physiology Swedish University of Agricultural